    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_1ecce5146e725376c68c30614e1db4db4843c6e9f000519bffb8fc6d6bd43086",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The proof proceeds by preserving the multiplicative constraint while changing its representation: time averaging selects equal-product tuples; Perron kernels move the hard cutoffs into contour variables; primewise factorization splits the resulting Dirichlet series into pairwise zeta poles and a regular Euler product; leading-pole extraction isolates a_k; and geometric-series coefficients encode the remaining integral as nonnegative matrices whose margins satisfy the cutoff capacities.",
