    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_7bc0e69889846aabe9f67be4a97aa547b39d831e5928ee7e70a3e558bae3b436",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "For the truncated zeta Dirichlet-polynomial moments, the equal-product Dirichlet series separates into pairwise zeta singularities and a regular Euler product; leading-order extraction evaluates the regular factor at the origin as a_k, while geometric-series coefficients and Perron cutoffs turn the residual contour into the capacity-constrained matrix count G_k(log X). Together with the stated leading term a_k vol(P_k), this explains the coefficient as prime-local arithmetic times substochastic-polytope volume.",
