    {
      "object_id": "mathia_synthesis_cfc664c8a2d1ffbabc4c5f17d3caaf678948d20aaec45274ddcfaf3f9671a230",
      "object_role": "synthesis",
      "proposed_content": "The unitary secular-coefficient identity and the zeta contour expansion reach the same transportation-table representation by different routes: secular-coefficient exponents prescribe row and column margins, whereas pairwise geometric-series exponents form a matrix whose margins are tested by Perron cutoffs. Truncating the secular-coefficient polynomial and imposing the zeta cutoffs both relax fixed margins to row-and-column capacity bounds, producing G_k.",
